Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add design note: paste a table into a table cell
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design note for issue #528. Pasting a table while the caret is inside a
table cell does not nest it — the paste path (insertBlocks) uses the
body-only getBlockIndex + insertBlockAt, and EditContext has no cell value,
so a cell target is never resolved and nothing is inserted. The Insert
Table command already handles this: it detects the cell via
getActiveLayout().blockParentMap and routes to insertTableInCell (the
cell-aware store.insertBlockAfter).

The note proposes applying the same cell detection in insertBlocks' single-
table branch — insert into the cell via insertBlockAfter when the caret is
in a cell, keep the body path otherwise — and flags deep id regeneration for
the pasted table's cell blocks (overlaps with #333). Design-note-first;
implementation to follow on this branch.
